# Implementation Plan - SPMS SSO Integration

This plan outlines the design and implementation for integrating SPMS SSO (Single Sign-On) with the Mail Automation system. Mail Automation will remain a standalone system, but it will trust SPMS as an identity provider (IdP). Users logged into SPMS can access Mail Automation without logging in again, and SPMS can synchronize user accounts with Mail Automation.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The database changes will add new fields (`authProvider`, `externalProvider`, and `lastSSOLogin`) to `User`, `Admin`, and `Employee` models. A database migration will be run to apply these changes to PostgreSQL.

> [!NOTE]
> Since `Admin` and `Employee` models require a password in the database, auto-created SSO users will be initialized with a secure, random bcrypt-hashed password so they cannot be logged in locally without resetting their password.

